mod:retyped_pointer_freeze;
// A POINTER A CAST RETYPED KEEPS ITS FREEZE (DEF-585; landing 177d2b4, row 7): each module one face, refused where what holds the `List` is
// replaced or grown while the pointer is held. A cast that changes the pointee (`=>! any->` and back to another type, a struct, the place's
// own type; on the caller's side, in a callee that passes it out by its `retypes` flag, through a second call, a parameter, an aggregate or a
// temporary) is taken to point into any `List` under its place. A `=>! wild`/`wildx` crossing that keeps its pointee keeps its type: the
// `wild` slot that can take it is read in (`xw3`, `xw5`, `np1`), and two crossings of different pointees meet as unknown (`jn1`, `jn2`).
// The flag climbs to its fixpoint (`cc2`, `cc12`, `cc16`, `cc24`, `cy1`) and keeps a retype met with a crossing (`ab1`) or a plain pass
// (`fj1`); a target written through a retyped call result is the List's (`g1`). On 58cab5a each fault is 236 at -O0 and -O2, and 97 under
// the freed-heap detector. DEF-639 (LOW, made by this row): `p639a` and `p639b` are right programs, refused because a write on the
// retyped pointer's own road conflicts with the coarse view it raised; its lift is 177d2b5's.
error:E5;
